# Fixture: the provider also passes a non-GPU device through vfio-pci — here an
# SR-IOV NIC (15b3:1017, Mellanox). Normal on a virtualization host, and nothing
# this playbook manages: 15b3:1017 is not in lium_cc_gpu_pci_ids or
# lium_nvswitch_pci_ids, so it can never appear in present_pci_ids and can never
# be verified against lspci.
#
# The managed ids are also written in UPPER CASE here, deliberately. vfio-pci
# parses them with %x, so `10DE:2335` is a working configuration a provider can
# and does type — and an exact-string comparison reads every one of them as an
# id that vanished, refusing on a host where nothing is wrong at all.
#
# It is NOT a narrowing. The role must converge, and must carry the id into the
# list it writes — `vfio-pci.ids=` is a module parameter whose last occurrence
# wins, so a drop-in listing only the ids we discovered would unbind the NIC.
GRUB_DEFAULT=0
GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX="kvm_intel.tdx=on vfio-pci.ids=10DE:2335,10DE:22A3,15b3:1017"
GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT="intel_iommu=on iommu=pt nohibernate"
